  "metadata": {
    "job": "Carved shop sign",
    "revision": "A",
    "notes": "The same 60° bit does two different jobs: v-carve varies its depth with the width of each letter, while chamfer follows the border at one fixed depth to break the edge. Both run before the profile — once the board is cut free it is loose on the spoilboard."
  },
